      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "adopt-methodology-from-source"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "The general process for turning a shared paper, book or standard into an adopted methodology: establish origin and licence, ingest the source, find and summarize related work items and issues and ask whether to coordinate, render the method with its adopted and refused parts, place it by ownership, integrate it by calling existing processes, give every tool it uses a Tool node, and put it to the owner. Process: library/processes/methodology-from-source.bpmn."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "adopt-methodology-from-source",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/library/skills/library-core/adopt-methodology-from-source.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/agent-memory",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "agent-memory"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Durable memory for a subagent — the three entry labels and what each promises, why entries are authored as graph nodes rather than in the generated file, the injection budget that silently truncates, and archiving as the third state between \"reaches everybody\" and \"deleted\"."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "agent-memory",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/conduct-core/agent-memory.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/agent-permissions",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "agent-permissions"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Securing what a coding agent may do without asking, from the person who can grant it: the `secure-agent-permissions` sub-process, run at session start and on demand when an action is denied. Vendor-neutral: the coding agent is a Tool (Claude Code is one; Gemini CLI, Cursor, Copilot and Codex are others), and each Tool's own config format belongs to its adapter, not here. Covers the permissions the harness's processes need, least privilege, how each one is explained before it is granted, how a grant is recorded, and the rules that no grant relaxes: never self-granted, generated projections are CI's, and merging to main is never a standing permission."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "agent-permissions",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/conduct-core/agent-permissions.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/archimate-models",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "archimate-models"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "ArchiMate models as knowledge-graph content: how a layer declares the Archi models it holds, what the `archimate` subgraph gives every model, view, element and relationship (an IRI, a thin page, and every view drawn as SVG from the model's own diagram, and its metamodel derived and checked), how to version the models, how to wire them into a folio's staging build and navbar, how to count and lower the crossed lines in a view before committing it, why every view carries a plain-language key, why names are the source's own terms linked to their SKOS concepts, and why no Java, no Archi CLI and no Archi HTML report is ever part of the pipeline. Read before adding, authoring, publishing or rendering an `.archimate` file, before citing an ArchiMate element from prose, and before reaching for Archi's own tooling in CI."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "archimate-models",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/ui/ui-core/archimate-models.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/artefact-reachability",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "artefact-reachability"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Which declared executable artefacts can be reached — decision tables, BPMN diagrams, self-declared entry points. Read before trusting that a .dmn works because it loads, before concluding a script has a caller, and before building any reachability report: load is not evaluability, a test is not a caller, and where a grep fails in both directions the subject has to be narrowed rather than the signals."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "artefact-reachability",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/kg/kg-core/artefact-reachability.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills/ask-the-person",
      "@type": "skos:Concept",
      "skos:inScheme": {
        "@id": "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/v0/ns/glossary/kg-skills"
      },
      "skos:prefLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "ask-the-person"
        }
      ],
      "skos:definition": [
        {
          "@value": "Put one question or decision to a person: the full question, context and every option written in the chat FIRST, then the same options as a tappable card. Use before every AskUserQuestion, request_decision / Decision card, button card, or any ask that hands a choice to the owner. Input is the composed question; output is the answer, or the default taken."
        }
      ],
      "skos:notation": "ask-the-person",
      "dcterms:source": "cat-harness/skills/conduct/conduct-core/ask-the-person.md",
      "skos:note": "candidate"
    },
    {
